===Other territories===
*{{flag|Australia}}. [[Ashmore and Cartier Islands]] - Special authorisation required.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.environment.gov.au/resource/ashmore-reef-and-cartier-island-marine-reserves-information-visitors |title=Ashmore Reef and Cartier Island Marine Reserves - Information for Visitors |access-date=August 4, 2017}}</ref>
*{{flagicon|Argentina}} [[Isla Apipé]] and Isla del Medio - By being Argentine territories, the same visa policy applies.
*{{flagicon|Crimea}} [[Crimea]]. Visa not required. Territory accessed under Russian visa policy.<ref>[http://www.themoscowtimes.com/news/article/foreigners-now-need-russian-visa-to-visit-crimea/497173.html Foreigners Now Need Russian Visa to Visit Crimea]</ref>
*{{flag|China}}. [[Hainan]] - 30 days; Visa-free for Brazilian nationals.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.nia.gov.cn/News/news/content.jsp?id=1646389 | title=Announcement from the National Immigration Administration on Implementing a Visa-Free Policy for Tourists from 59 Countries in Hainan Province}}</ref>
*{{flag|China}}. [[Tibet Autonomous Region]] - Tibet Travel Permit required (10 [[USD]]). = [https://www.yalaadventure.com/tibet How to get Tibet Travel Permit], Successful Application Tips<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.tibettravelplanner.com/travel_permit.htm |title=How to get a Tibet Travel Permits - Tibet Visa 2016? |access-date=2014-03-24 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171022061211/http://www.tibettravelplanner.com/travel_permit.htm |archive-date=2017-10-22 |url-status=dead}}</ref>
*{{flag|Colombia}}. [[San Andrés Island|San Andrés]] and [[Leticia, Amazonas|Leticia]] - Visitors arriving at [[Gustavo Rojas Pinilla International Airport]] and [[Alfredo Vásquez Cobo International Airport]] must buy tourist cards on arrival.
*{{flag|Ecuador}}. [[File:Bandera Província Galápagos.svg|border|22x20px]] [[Galapagos Province|Galápagos]] - 60 days; Visitors must pre-register to receive a 20 USD Transit Control Card (TCT).<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.gobiernogalapagos.gob.ec/para-ingresar-a-la-provincia-de-galapagos/ | title=Para ingresar a la provincia de Galapagos}}</ref>
*{{flag|Eritrea}} outside [[Asmara]] - To travel in the rest of the country, a Travel Permit for Foreigners is required (20 [[Eritrean nakfa]]).<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.eritrea.be/MoT.htm|title = Ministry of Tourism - Tourism Service Center}}</ref>
*{{flag|Fiji}}. [[Lau Province]] - Special permission required.<ref>{{cite web|title=Fiji Country Specific Information|url=http://www.travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_1114.html#entry_requirements|publisher=Bureau of Consular Affairs, U.S. Department of State|access-date=18 November 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131102204202/http://travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_1114.html#entry_requirements|archive-date=2 November 2013|url-status=dead|df=dmy-all}}</ref>
*{{flagicon|Greece}} [[File:Flag of the Greek Orthodox Church.svg|21px]] [[Mount Athos]] - Special permit required (4 days: 25 [[euro]] for [[Eastern Orthodox Church|Orthodox]] visitors, 35 [[euro]] for non-Orthodox visitors, 18 [[euro]] for students). There is a visitors' quota: maximum 100 [[Eastern Orthodox Church|Orthodox]] and 10 non-Orthodox per day and women are not allowed.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.athosfriends.org/PilgrimsGuide/planning/ |title=The Friends of Mount Athos - A Pilgrim's Guide to Mount Athos: Planning Your Visit |access-date=2014-03-24 |archive-date=2017-12-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171201154734/http://athosfriends.org/PilgrimsGuide/planning/ |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.mountathosinfos.gr/pages/agionoros/pilgrims_info.en.html |title=Mount Athos Infos . Gr |access-date=2014-03-24 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20071201150655/http://www.mountathosinfos.gr/pages/agionoros/pilgrims_info.en.html |archive-date=2007-12-01 |url-status=dead }}</ref>
*{{flag|India}}. Protected Area Permit (PAP) required for whole states of [[Nagaland]] and [[Sikkim]] and parts of states [[Manipur]], [[Arunachal Pradesh]], [[Uttaranchal]], [[Jammu and Kashmir (union territory)|Jammu and Kashmir]], [[Rajasthan]], [[Himachal Pradesh]]. Restricted Area Permit (RAP) required for all of [[Andaman and Nicobar Islands]] and parts of [[Sikkim]]. Some of these requirements are occasionally lifted for a year.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.timaticweb.com/cgi-bin/tim_website_client.cgi?FullText=1&COUNTRY=IN&SECTION=VI&SUBSECTION=00&user=KLMB2C&subuser=KLMB2C |title=Visa information |access-date=2013-12-17 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20140314003632/https://www.timaticweb.com/cgi-bin/tim_website_client.cgi?FullText=1&COUNTRY=IN&SECTION=VI&SUBSECTION=00&user=KLMB2C&subuser=KLMB2C |archive-date=2014-03-14 |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://as.and.nic.in/TourismAND/TCorner/ForeignersNew.htm |title=Entry Formalities to Andaman |access-date=November 26, 2013 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120426085021/http://as.and.nic.in/TourismAND/TCorner/ForeignersNew.htm |archive-date=April 26, 2012 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://arunachaltourism.com/entry_formalities.php |title=Arunachal Tourism |access-date=August 1, 2014 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140701111837/http://arunachaltourism.com/entry_formalities.php |archive-date=July 1, 2014 }}</ref><ref>{{dead link|date=May 2016}}{{cite web|url=http://manipurbhawan.nic.in/entryformalities.htm |title=Entry Formalities in Manipur |access-date=August 4, 2015 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110809003009/http://manipurbhawan.nic.in/entryformalities.htm |archive-date=August 9, 2011 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://manipurhub.com/news/manipur/protected-area-permit-requirement-lifted-from-manipur-for-one-year/ |access-date=August 4, 2015 |title=时时彩平台推广&#124;时时彩平台推广官网【Pk彩票官方授权】 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190329112747/http://manipurhub.com/news/manipur/protected-area-permit-requirement-lifted-from-manipur-for-one-year/ |archive-date=March 29, 2019 |url-status=dead |df=mdy-all }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://lakshadweeptourism.nic.in/web9.htm |title=Tourism in Lakshadweep |access-date=2014-08-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140713171604/http://lakshadweeptourism.nic.in/web9.htm |archive-date=2014-07-13 |url-status=dead }}</ref>
*{{flag|Iraqi Kurdistan}} - 30 days; Visitors may apply for an e-Visa.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://evisa-iraq.org/eligible-countries/ | title=Iraqi Kurdistan e-Visa}}</ref>
*{{flag|Iran}}. [[Kish Island]] - Visa not required.<ref>{{cite web|title=Iran Country Specific Information |url=http://www.travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_1142.html#entry_requirements |publisher=Bureau of Consular Affairs, U.S. Department of State |access-date=18 November 2013 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131203094257/http://www.travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_1142.html |archive-date=December 3, 2013 }}</ref>
*{{flag|Kazakhstan}}. Closed cities - Special permission required for the town of [[Baikonur]] and surrounding areas in [[Kyzylorda Oblast]], and the town of [[Gvardeyskiy, Kazakhstan|Gvardeyskiy]] near [[Almaty]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Kazakhstan Country Specific Information |url=http://www.travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_1150.html#entry_requirements |publisher=Bureau of Consular Affairs, U.S. Department of State |access-date=18 November 2013 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131102170930/http://travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_1150.html |archive-date=November 2, 2013 }}</ref>
*{{flag|North Korea}} outside [[Pyongyang]] - Special permit required. People are not allowed to leave the capital city, tourists can only leave the capital with a governmental tourist guide (no independent moving).
*{{flag|Malaysia}}. {{flag|Sabah}} and {{flag|Sarawak}} - Visa not required. These states have their own immigration authorities and passport is required to travel to them, however the same visa applies.<ref>{{cite web|title=Malaysia Country Specific Information |url=http://www.travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_960.html#entry_requirements |publisher=Bureau of Consular Affairs, U.S. Department of State |access-date=18 November 2013 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131128154523/http://travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_960.html |archive-date=November 28, 2013}}</ref>
*{{flag|Russia}}. Special authorization required for several [[Russian closed city|closed cities and regions in Russia]] require special authorization.<ref>{{cite web|title=Russian Federation Country Specific Information|url=http://www.travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_1006.html#entry_requirements|publisher=Bureau of Consular Affairs, U.S. Department of State|access-date=18 November 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131203003453/http://www.travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_1006.html#entry_requirements|archive-date=3 December 2013|url-status=dead|df=dmy-all}}</ref>
*{{flagicon|Saudi Arabia}} [[Mecca]] and [[Medina]] - Special access required. Non-Muslims and those following the [[Ahmadiyya]] religious movement are strictly prohibited from entry.
*{{flag|Sudan}}. [[Darfur]] - Separate travel permit is required.<ref>{{cite web|title=Republic of South Sudan Country Specific Information|url=https://travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_5525.html#entry_requirements|publisher=Bureau of Consular Affairs, U.S. Department of State|access-date=19 November 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131105150822/http://travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_5525.html#entry_requirements|archive-date=5 November 2013|url-status=dead|df=dmy-all}}</ref>
*{{flag|Sudan}} outside [[Khartoum]] - All foreigners traveling more than 25 kilometers outside of [[Khartoum]] must obtain a travel permit.
*{{flag|Tajikistan}}. [[Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Province]] - OIVR permit required (15+5 [[Tajikistani Somoni]]) and another special permit (free of charge) is required for [[Lake Sarez]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.pamirs.org/visas.htm |title=Pamirs - the roof of the world |access-date=2014-03-24 |archive-date=2017-06-30 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170630035659/http://www.pamirs.org/visas.htm |url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://tajiktourism.com/tajikistan-visa/ |title=Tajikistan Visa &#124; Tajik Tourism |access-date=2014-03-24 |archive-date=2017-07-06 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170706121812/http://tajiktourism.com/tajikistan-visa/ |url-status=dead}}</ref>
*{{flag|Turkmenistan}}. Closed cities - A special permit, issued prior to arrival by Ministry of Foreign Affairs, is required if visiting the following places: [[Atamurat]], [[Cheleken]], [[Dashoguz]], [[Serakhs]] and [[Serhetabat]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.timaticweb.com/cgi-bin/tim_website_client.cgi?FullText=1&COUNTRY=TM&SECTION=VI&SUBSECTION=AI&user=KLMB2C&subuser=KLMB2C |title=Visa information |access-date=2016-01-11 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20140314003610/https://www.timaticweb.com/cgi-bin/tim_website_client.cgi?FullText=1&COUNTRY=TM&SECTION=VI&SUBSECTION=AI&user=KLMB2C&subuser=KLMB2C |archive-date=2014-03-14 |url-status=dead}}</ref>
*{{flag|United States}}. [[United States Minor Outlying Islands]] - Special permits required for [[Baker Island]], [[Howland Island]], [[Jarvis Island]], [[Johnston Atoll]], [[Kingman Reef]], [[Midway Atoll]], [[Palmyra Atoll]] and [[Wake Island]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.fws.gov/bakerisland/visit.html |title=Visiting - Baker Island National Wildlife Refuge |access-date=November 16, 2013 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131017211743/http://www.fws.gov/bakerisland/visit.html |archive-date=October 17, 2013}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.fws.gov/howlandisland/visit.html |title=Visiting Howland National Wildlife Refuge |access-date=November 16, 2013 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131017212340/http://www.fws.gov/howlandisland/visit.html |archive-date=October 17, 2013}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.fws.gov/jarvisisland/ |title=Welcome to Jarvis Island National Wildlife Refuge |access-date=March 4, 2012 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120328143327/http://www.fws.gov/jarvisisland/ |archive-date=March 28, 2012}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.fws.gov/johnstonisland/visit.html |title=Visiting Johnston Atoll National Wildlife Refuge |access-date=November 16, 2013 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130607120346/http://www.fws.gov/johnstonisland/visit.html |archive-date=June 7, 2013}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.fws.gov/kingmanreef/visit.html |title=Visiting Kingman Reef National Wildlife Refuge |access-date=November 16, 2013 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131017212056/http://www.fws.gov/kingmanreef/visit.html |archive-date=October 17, 2013}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.fws.gov/midway/visit.html |title=Visiting Midway Atoll National Wildlife Refuge |access-date=May 12, 2014 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140227230950/http://www.fws.gov/midway/visit.html |archive-date=February 27, 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.fws.gov/palmyraatoll/visit.html |title=Visiting - Palmyra National Wildlife Refuge |access-date=November 16, 2013 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130522074332/http://www.fws.gov/palmyraatoll/visit.html |archive-date=May 22, 2013}}</ref>
*{{flag|Venezuela}}. [[Margarita Island]] - Visa not required. All visitors are fingerprinted.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://travel.state.gov/content/passports/en/country/venezuela.html |title=Venezuela |access-date=2016-06-12 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150930232933/http://travel.state.gov/content/passports/en/country/venezuela.html |archive-date=2015-09-30 |url-status=dead}}</ref>
*{{flag|Vietnam}}. [[Phú Quốc]] - Visa not required for 30 days.<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://www.vietseatourist.vn/News/category1/news-57/No-visa-required-for-tourists-to-Phu-Quoc-on-short-stay.html |title=No visa required for tourists to Phu Quoc on short stay - Vietsea Tourist - Travel to Vietnam, Laos, Cambodia and Thailand &#124; Vietnam Travel Tours |access-date=2014-03-24 |archive-date=2017-07-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170701095940/http://www.vietseatourist.vn/News/category1/news-57/No-visa-required-for-tourists-to-Phu-Quoc-on-short-stay.html |url-status=dead }}</ref>
*{{flag|Yemen}} outside [[Sanaa]] or [[Aden]] - Special permission needed for travel outside Sanaa or Aden.<ref>{{cite web|title=Yemen Country Specific Information |url=http://www.travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_1061.html#entry_requirements |publisher=Bureau of Consular Affairs, U.S. Department of State |access-date=19 November 2013 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131114101625/http://travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_1061.html |archive-date=November 14, 2013}}</ref>
*{{flagicon|United Nations}} [[United Nations Buffer Zone in Cyprus|UN Buffer Zone in Cyprus]] - Access Permit is required for travelling inside the zone, except Civil Use Areas.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.unficyp.org/nqcontent.cfm?a_id=1608&tt=graphic&lang=l1 |title=UNFICYP > Buffer Zone Permits |access-date=2014-08-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141021143210/http://www.unficyp.org/nqcontent.cfm?a_id=1608&tt=graphic&lang=l1 |archive-date=2014-10-21 |url-status=dead}}</ref>
*{{flagicon|United Nations}} [[Korean Demilitarized Zone]] - Restricted area.
*{{flagicon|United Nations}} [[UNDOF Zone]] and [[Ghajar]] - Restricted area.

